"FX-26's table keyed by pairs' identity, which KFX has not yet: a list
 seen as a union's value might be rebuilt in Rust, a new pair where FX-26
 has the old one (C194; the Fixpt team's TODO §36, until the emitter shows
 no conversion copies a pair at a region that may be written)."
(define-effect kfx (maxeff (read @globals) (alloc @t) (alloc @k) (read @t) (write @t) (write @k) spin))
(define main (subr kfx () i64)
  (lambda ()
    (let ((t (the (eqtable (pairof int int @k) int @k @t) (make-eqtable (pair-identity))))
          (p (the (pairof int int @k) (cons 1 2))))
      (begin (eqtable-set! t p 5) (int->i64 (eqtable-ref t p 0))))))
